{
  "summary": "The experiment tested image_only data with multiprofile settings using ResNet-50, achieving validation accuracy of 0.328 and F1 of 0.288, significantly lower than RNA-only multiprofile baselines (e.g., 0.650). This suggests multiprofile benefits may not generalize to image data, but the impact of image encoder choice and aggregation methods remains uncertain without direct comparisons to other modalities or configurations."
}

